# g96-fu-misc wiring (lead)

## 1. Refused relay frame toast (deferred-g95 item 5)

File: native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs, directly after the line
`built_remote.events.bind_pc_access(pc_access.clone()).map_err(|_| ComposeError::AlreadyBound("PC access events"))?;`

    // The relay's refusal of an oversize frame is announced on the app feed as ui/relayPayloadRefused {bytes, limit} (Node's relay-payload-refused).
    let app_announcer = domain_inputs.config.clone();
    built_remote.events.bind_app_feed(Arc::new(move |method, params| app_announcer.announce(method, params))).map_err(|_| ComposeError::AlreadyBound("app feed of the remote events"))?;

(`domain_inputs.config` is the `Config` compose_domains_pre binds with `announce_to`; if the name differs at that point, use the same Config handle.)
No new Cargo edge (mixdog-app-server-daemon already depends on mixdog-core-config). Nothing to remove from SERVICE_PENDING.

## 2. Login-shell environment (item 6)

Done in lib.rs run(): nothing to wire. After x-residual-moves-b-client keeps the coverage of the Electron main process's own children
(ssh tunnels, the core spawn) it deletes the TypeScript read.
